<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <!-- Distributed from 0.4.0. It was held back as spike-stage from Phase 316, which had
         the effect that no domain workspace could consume the engine at all — the one
         domain using it reached across a sibling checkout for a byte-copy of its output.
         The engine is domain-generic by construction (a vocabulary is a plain `Idl` value
         a caller supplies), so shipping it is what makes a second vocabulary declarable
         without the declarer living in this repo. See DECISIONS.md D14. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Fuaran.Core.Idl</PackageId>
    <Description>Fuaran.Core.Idl — the interface-definition engine: a typed model of a domain's node vocabulary (kinds, unions, enums, records, four-way optionality, a declarable node envelope, hosted slots) plus the legs generated from it — a schema-driven canonical encoder/decoder, an F# structural-layer emitter with a declared-support channel (docs, splices, host projections), a JSON-schema emitter, a stability diff classifier over two artifact revisions, and the codegen trust boundary (allowlisted `Custom` resolution, sanitisation). The engine only; a vocabulary is DATA a domain declares and owns in its own repo. FSharp.Core + Fuaran.Core.Wire only.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Idl.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Diff.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Trust.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Fuaran.Core.Wire\Fuaran.Core.Wire.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
